o allowing subject to be present at your operation (26 TAC §745.641)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250709-v9","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5625-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250709","date":"2025-07-09","original_code":"746.5625(b)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-08-13","finding":"Electronic Child Safety Alarm - installed and maintained according to manufacturer's instructions: During the inspection, the electronic child safety alarm in the school vehicle was not working.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026488561","violation_type_title":"Electronic Child Safety Alarm - installed and maintained according to manufacturer's instructions (26 TAC §746.5625(b))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250529","date":"2025-05-29","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":3,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905953867","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905953867","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2025-05-29","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250529-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250529","date":"2025-05-29","original_code":"746.1201(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-07-09","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Relate to Children: This standard was evaluated as part of a DFPS investigation and was found to be deficient. It was determined a caregiver was not patient with an infant who would not eat from a bottle.  The caregiver moved the infant from side to side in a jerking motion, causing the infant to hit their head. The caregiver was forcing the bottle in the infant's mouth when the infant did not want to take it.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026611136","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Relate to Children (26 TAC §746.1201(2))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250529-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2805","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250529","date":"2025-05-29","original_code":"746.2805","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-07-09","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - No Harsh, Cruel or Unusual: This standard was evaluated as part of a DFPS investigation and was found to be deficient. It was determined a caregiver harshly moved children and set them down abruptly. This continued a minimum of 5 minutes with 3 different children.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026611135","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - No Harsh, Cruel or Unusual (26 TAC §746.2805)","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250529-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2401-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250529","date":"2025-05-29","original_code":"746.2401(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-07-09","finding":"Basic Requirements for Infants - Holding and Comforting: This standard was evaluated as part of a DFPS investigation and was found to be deficient. It was determined through staff interviews that an infant who was crying throughout the day was not comforted by the caregiver.  In addition, in the video obtained during the investigation, the caregiver sets an infant down while the infant is upset.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026611137","violation_type_title":"Basic Requirements for Infants - Holding and Comforting (26 TAC §746.2401(3))","topic_label":"Other"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250528-2","date":"2025-05-28","inspection_type":"Insp