-10","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - Grabbing and Pulling: This standard was evaluated as part of an investigation by the Department of Family and Protective Services and was found to be deficient. A caregiver used inappropriate physical force by grabbing a child?s arm, which caused visible injury. This type of physical action is not allowed and is considered overly aggressive in a childcare setting.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026610730","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - Grabbing and Pulling (26 TAC §746.2805(3))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250219-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2803-4-c","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250219","date":"2025-02-19","original_code":"746.2803(4)(C)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-04-10","finding":"Positive Methods of Discipline and Guidance - Redirecting Behavior: This standard was evaluated as part of an investigation by the Department of Family and Protective Services and was found to be deficient. A caregiver attempted to manage a child's behavior through physical intervention rather than using encouraging, constructive methods. The action lacked the positive guidance strategies that help build a child?s confidence and ability to self-regulate.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026610731","violation_type_title":"Positive Methods of Discipline and Guidance - Redirecting Behavior (26 TAC §746.2803(4)(C))","topic_label":"Other"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250219-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1495877-i20250219","date":"2025-02-19","original_code":"746.1201(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-04-10","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Relate to Children: This standard was evaluated as part of an investigation by the Department of Family and 